  "body": {
    "id": "lem:branch-reduction",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For either \\(r=\\mathrm{SDC}\\) or \\(r=\\mathrm{LEI}\\), every \\(Q\\in\\mathcal Q^r(P)\\) induces, for each arm \\(a\\), a sign \\(b\\in\\{-1,+1\\}\\) and missing-cell means \\(x_a\\in\\mathcal F_{a,b}^r(P)\\) such that \\(\\theta_a(Q)=c_a+\\sum_{j\\in\\mathcal M_a}p_jx_{a,j}\\). Conversely, every vector in \\(\\mathcal F_{a,b}^r(P)\\) is realized by a bounded missing-cell completion satisfying the branch score inequalities; exact aggregate support is addressed by Theorem 1.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "r",
      "Q",
      "Qclass",
